Third-party components and data (not covered by this licence):
- NeRF-synthetic "lego" (Mildenhall et al., 2020) and Mip-NeRF 360 "bonsai" (Barron et al., 2022) are
  downloaded at first run from public mirrors under their authors' terms; the demo scenes in
  web/scenes/ are Gaussian-splat models trained from them and carry the same attribution.
- COLMAP / pycolmap: BSD-3-Clause. LPIPS: BSD-2-Clause (its VGG/AlexNet backbones come from
  torchvision). Triton: MIT. PyTorch: BSD-3-Clause.
- The training method follows Kerbl et al., "3D Gaussian Splatting for Real-Time Radiance Field
  Rendering" (SIGGRAPH 2023). This repository is an independent implementation; it contains no code
  from the Inria reference implementation (which has its own non-commercial licence).
